{
 "id": "vision_lighting",
 "version": "1.0.0",
 "depends_on": [],
 "description": "LIGHTING / APPEARANCE INVARIANCE (FRONTIER T3) -- the illuminant as a low-D CROSS-FRAME map, discovered and factored, with recognition invariant to what it leaves fixed. An ObjSurface carries integer cones (cL,cM,cS) = reflectance x illuminant: the reflectance is the stable IN-FRAME property (integer lattice), the illuminant a diagonal (von Kries) CROSS-FRAME map. li_frame_stats reads the frame's OWN per-channel anchor (max) and sum (hub-scoped via Neighbours, no global grab); li_inclass DISCOVERS whether the change is in-class by an ORDER-STATISTIC CONSISTENCY test needing no surface correspondence, and mints an Illuminant holding the gain as an exact (numer,denom) pair -- refusing a spatially-varying change outright; li_mint MDL-mints a SurfaceIdentity (m_min=2 FALLS OUT of d=3) carrying the prototype AND its frame's anchor; li_recognize matches by ANCHOR-RELATIVE reflectance via exact integer cross-multiplication (the illuminant cancels identically); li_raw_recognize is the no-discounting RAW BASELINE control. NO new Rust: reuses Count/Filter/NodesOfType/Neighbours/MaxOver/Sum/Exists/Not/Eq/Gt/Lt/Times/And + run_rules. NO magic number: the anchor is the frame's own measured ceiling, m_min falls out of d=3, and every comparison is exact integer cross-multiplication (no threshold, no tolerance). BOUNDED: the DIAGONAL illuminant class ONLY -- multi-illuminant scenes, shadows, penumbrae and spatially-varying light are NOT solved, only REFUSED (the NAMED FRONTIER); the global reflectance/illuminant ambiguity is intrinsic and unresolved by construction. Flag-gated on LightingParams.lighting, OFF by default (sec 9 -- default 0 => byte-identical, seed inert). See VISION_LIGHTING_PREREG.md.",
 "microtheory": {
  "id": "vision_lighting_mt",
  "label": "lighting/appearance invariance: the illuminant as a discovered low-D cross-frame map, factored by an anchor-relative code"
 },
