   "name": "li_frame_stats",
   "comment": "The frame's OWN per-channel order statistics: the ANCHOR a_ch = MaxOver(frame's surfaces, c_ch) and the SUM s_ch = Sum(...). Scoped by Neighbours(frame,'has_surface') -- the frame's own population, NOT a global NodesOfType grab (VISION_PROTOCOL sec 12.1). The anchor is the frame's MEASURED dynamic-range ceiling, which under a diagonal illuminant scales exactly with the illuminant -- so dividing by it makes the appearance code RELATIVE, which is sec 13's whole corollary (ratios transfer, absolutes do not). NO constant is introduced. The stats_done guard makes the rule fire once per frame so run_rules converges. Flag-gated, OFF by default (sec 9).",
