  {
   "name": "li_inclass",
   "comment": "DISCOVERS whether the lighting change between this frame and its reference frame is IN-CLASS (a diagonal / von Kries map). The test is an ORDER-STATISTIC CONSISTENCY: under a diagonal map every statistic scales by the same per-channel gain, so anchor:sum must agree between the frames on ALL THREE channels (exact integer cross-multiplication). It requires NO surface correspondence -- so it is not circular with recognition, which is what it gates. If it HOLDS: mint an Illuminant carrying the discovered gain as an exact (numer,denom) PAIR per channel (the ratio is the CROSS-FRAME map, held intensionally -- never divided into a float, per the frame/continuum invariant) and set illum_inclass=1. If it FAILS: nothing is minted and illum_inclass stays 0, so li_recognize cannot fire -- a spatially-varying (multi-illuminant) change is REFUSED rather than blindly normalised. That refusal is the whole difference between an invariance and a universal container (sec 1.1). Flag-gated, OFF by default (sec 9).",
