   "comment": "DYNAMIC QUANTIZATION (mint) of a SurfaceIdentity from the REFERENCE frame. Gates: (1) lighting>0.5; (2) THE MDL GATE -- Count(surfaces in this frame with the same EXACT cone triple) >= 2 = m_min, which FALLS OUT of d=3 (a prototype costs d integers and saves d-1 per member, so it pays iff m > d/(d-1) = 1.5, i.e. m >= 2 -- NO magic number, VISION_PROTOCOL sec 13); (3) the CANONICAL-REPRESENTATIVE guard -- only the min-sidx member of a cone triple may mint, so under batch tick exactly ONE identity per distinct reflectance is minted; (4) Not(Exists SurfaceIdentity at this triple) -- recognize-not-re-mint across passes. Effects: add the SurfaceIdentity carrying the prototype cones (pL,pM,pS) AND ITS OWN FRAME'S ANCHOR (paL,paM,paS) -- the anchor must travel with the prototype, because the invariant is the reflectance RELATIVE to the frame it was seen in. UNSUPERVISED: no label is read. Flag-gated, OFF by default (sec 9).",
